# netsurf: <slot>.assignedNodes / assignedElements and assignedSlot (patch 486)
# Generated 2026-11-27
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 485)
#
# A <slot> had no assignedNodes / assignedElements and nothing had an
# assignedSlot (an interface-census stub answered null): lit's
# @queryAssignedElements and the components that read their slotted
# children threw "not a function" -- old.reddit.com's login components (15
# such errors a load at 485, and the faceplate-enter listener threw 3
# times).
#
# vita_polyfill.js: a host's light child is assigned to the first <slot> in
# its shadow tree whose name is its slot attribute (text, and elements
# without one, to the default slot). assignedNodes({flatten}) follows a slot
# assigned to a slot and gives an empty slot's fallback; assignedElements
# keeps the elements; assignedSlot (elements and text) replaces the stub
# (closed roots answer null). A real <slot>'s chain here is the bridge's
# class prototype, not HTMLSlotElement's: the methods go there and on
# HTMLElement.prototype / HTMLSlotElement.prototype. Not here: slotchange.
#
# JS-slot-api.html: Chromium 8/8, 485 aborts, 486 8/8. old.reddit at 486:
# "not a function" 15 -> 4, rejections 15 -> 8, listener throws 3 -> 0.
